course: dictionary
lesson: 14813
title: Dazzling words: pyrotechnic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about fire, light and noise. Pyrotechnic is one of them. Look at the clues: «The pyrotechnic display lit up the whole night sky.» A display is a show, and the sky is lit up, so pyrotechnic must be about fireworks.
explain: Pyrotechnics, usually in the plural, means a fireworks show or the skill of making and setting off fireworks. «The pyrotechnics at the festival were loud and bright.» Try the swap check: put "fireworks" in place of pyrotechnics. The sentence still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: The word can also praise something that dazzles, even when there is no fire at all. «Her guitar playing was pyrotechnic, with fast, flashing notes.» Nobody is setting anything alight. The word means very brilliant and showy, as if the playing were a firework show. This is figurative language.
fact: Pyrotechnic means to do with fireworks.
fact: Pyrotechnics means a fireworks show, or the skill of making fireworks.
fact: Pyrotechnic can also mean very brilliant, dazzling and showy, especially in music, speech or skill.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «pyrotechnic display», «pyrotechnic show» and «verbal pyrotechnics».
exercise: «The pyrotechnic display lit up the night sky.» What does pyrotechnic mean here? | *To do with fireworks | To do with cooking | To do with swimming | To do with trains
exercise: «The pyrotechnics at the festival were loud and bright.» What are pyrotechnics here? | *A fireworks show | A busy market of food stalls | A quiet picnic in the park | A long parade of cars
exercise: «Her guitar playing was pyrotechnic, with fast, flashing notes.» What does pyrotechnic suggest about the playing? | *Brilliant and dazzling | Broken and out of tune | Slow and sleepy | Dark and quiet
test: «The magician's pyrotechnic show left the crowd gasping.» What does pyrotechnic mean here? | Hidden under the stage | Very cold | *Dazzling, like fireworks | Dull and grey
test: A reviewer wrote, «The speech was full of verbal pyrotechnics.» What is being praised? | Mumbled words nobody could hear | Lots of spelling mistakes | A long pause with no words at all | *Dazzling, clever and showy language
exam: Mia says, «Pyrotechnic is just a fancy word for loud.» Why is she wrong? | *It means to do with fireworks, and can also mean dazzling and showy | It means exactly the same as loud | It is a word only used in science | It is the name of a kind of food
